Scope
-----

This license covers the material in this repository, which comprises:

  * `packages/desktop-app/` and `packages/unity-plugin/` -- the application and
    the Unity Editor package.
  * `scripts/`, `tools/` and the root build configuration.
  * `Documentation/BUSY Bar API & Display Technical Developer Guide.md`,
    `Documentation/busy_bar_controller_studio.html`,
    `Documentation/hardware-samples/` and `Documentation/design-history/`.
  * `icon reference/` -- the original 16x16 source artwork. The third-party
    logos that folder's README describes are untracked and are not part of
    this repository.

It does not cover, and this project makes no claim over:

  * The BUSY Bar hardware, its firmware, and BUSY Bar's own documentation,
    OpenAPI specification and example applications. Those belong to their
    authors -- see https://github.com/busy-app. Local copies of that material,
    if present, live in `Documentation/private/`, which is untracked and never
    redistributed from here.
  * `Animations/` -- the LED animation frame sets. See the attribution below.
  * `packages/desktop-app/src/shared/busy-font.ts` -- the generated glyph
    table. See the attribution below.
  * Third-party trademarks and brand marks. Application names and logos appear
    only to identify the applications whose notifications this software
    displays; ownership remains with their respective holders.
  * Dependencies, which carry their own licenses.


Attribution
-----------

`Animations/` contains the LED animation frame sets from the BUSY Bar firmware
(`assets/animations/`), redistributed here unmodified.

  Copyright (c) 2024-2026 Flipper FZCO
  Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
  (CC-BY-SA-4.0) -- https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
  Source: https://github.com/busy-app/busybar-firmware

That is a different licence from the MIT terms above, and it carries a
ShareAlike condition: anyone who adapts these frames must license the adaptation
under CC-BY-SA-4.0 as well. Bundling them alongside this application does not
place the application under that licence, but modifying them does place the
result under it. If you fork this repository, keep this notice.

`packages/desktop-app/src/shared/busy-font.ts` is a generated glyph table: the
printable ASCII of the BUSY Bar firmware's own `lv_font_busy_regular_5`,
converted from its LVGL C source by `tools/lvgl-font-to-ts.js`. Only the pixel
data is reproduced -- no outlines and no font binary.

  Copyright (c) 2021 TakWolf -- https://ark-pixel-font.takwolf.com/
  Copyright (c) 2024-2026 Flipper FZCO
  Licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL-1.1)
  -- https://openfontlicense.org/
  Source: https://github.com/busy-app/busybar-firmware --
          `assets/frontend/assets/fonts/busy_regular_5px.ttf`, itself derived
          from the Ark Pixel Font, by way of the LVGL font generated from it at
          `lib/lvgl_addons/fonts/lv_font_busy_regular_5.c`

The firmware's own REUSE metadata annotates that `lib/lvgl_addons/**` directory
GPL-2.0-or-later, and the `busy_*` font assets OFL-1.1. The generated C carries
no SPDX header of its own, so it is worth being precise about which of the two
applies here: every glyph extracted is bit-identical to a direct rasterisation
of the OFL-licensed TTF at the same size, and none of Flipper's C -- no tables,
no structs, no source -- is reproduced. What is copied is the font's pixels, so
the licence that travels with them is the font's.

The OFL permits bundling a font with software under any licence, so this does
not place the application under the OFL -- but that one file stays OFL-licensed,
and the notice above must travel with it. The OFL also forbids selling the font
on its own, and requires that a modified version not be distributed under a
Reserved Font Name. If you fork this repository, keep this notice.
